<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Hawqal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 977 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Hawqal was a tenth-century Arab geographer and traveller. Writing around 977 CE, he described the king of Ghana as the wealthiest monarch on earth because of his gold. His account is an important early source for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a>'s economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-hawqal.jpg" alt="Ibn Hawqal" width="320" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Extracted (scanned) by Zereshk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ibn_Howqal_World_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
